tests/fixtures/watchdog/ — fixtures for scripts/watchdog.sh (#932)

launcher.sh   a model launcher: polls `watchdog.sh check` on a virtual clock
              (--now stepped by the poll interval). See its header.

The session layout the tests build by hand, and that `check` reads, is the one
Claude Code 2.1.329 writes, measured on 2026-11-20 (Issue-932 spike, U1-U3):

  <projects>/<slug>/<uuid>.jsonl                      the session transcript,
                                                      appended per record
  <projects>/<slug>/<uuid>/subagents/agent-<id>.jsonl a subagent's transcript;
                                                      it grows while the parent
                                                      file stands still
  <projects>/<slug>/<uuid>/subagents/agent-<id>.meta.json

  <uuid>      the session id: the launcher chooses it (`--session-id`), the
              session's commands see it as CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID, and a
              subagent's commands see the parent's
  <slug>      the launch directory with every non-alphanumeric character
              replaced by `-`; a launcher globs `*/<uuid>.jsonl` instead of
              rebuilding it
  <projects>  ~/.claude/projects

The transcript does not exist for the first 8-10 s of a session; `--since`
covers that window.

devagent's own half of the record (scripts/lib/heartbeat.sh):

  $(devagent_home)/state/watchdog/<uuid>/script             last devagent script entry
  $(devagent_home)/state/watchdog/<uuid>/dispatch           "v1 <project> <issue> <step number> <step name>"
  $(devagent_home)/state/watchdog/<uuid>/beat               last `watchdog.sh heartbeat`
  $(devagent_home)/state/watchdog/<uuid>/beat.window        "<seconds>", while a --silent gap is open
  $(devagent_home)/state/watchdog/<uuid>/wrap.<run>         last output of one wrapped run
  $(devagent_home)/state/watchdog/<uuid>/wrap.<run>.window  "<seconds>", while that run lives

Progress is each file's mtime; the tests set it with `touch -d @<epoch>`.
